# exit: 0
# The interactive front-ends keep the theories a `require' elaborates
# across the scope rebuild a LOAD does, so that reloading a file does
# not re-read everything under it. Whether that happened is not
# visible on the wire, and must not be: the contract is that a reload
# answers exactly what the first load answered. The two LOAD frames
# below are that contract -- same uuid, same tag, same goal -- and so
# are the two `print' frames, which read the served theory rather than
# the reloaded file.
LOAD "fixtures/sub/reload.ec" 7
print neighbour.
LOAD "fixtures/sub/reload.ec" 7
print neighbour.
